## Request Throughput

*Rates are the pooler's own per-snapshot averages over stats_period; the max is the highest snapshot average, not the busiest instant.*

| Metric         | Average | Max snapshot average |       At |
|----------------|--------:|---------------------:|---------:|
| Transactions/s |     1.5 |                    3 | 13:41:13 |
| Queries/s      |    10.5 |                   21 | 13:41:13 |
| Network in     | 646 B/s |            1.26 KB/s | 13:41:13 |
| Network out    | 283 B/s |              565 B/s | 13:41:13 |

## Query Timing

*Averages skip the snapshots that timed none and weight the rest by operation count; the max is the highest snapshot average, not a peak.*

| Metric           | Weighted average | Max snapshot average |       At |
|------------------|-----------------:|---------------------:|---------:|
| Transaction time |           2.0 ms |               2.0 ms | 13:41:13 |
| Query time       |          261 µs |              261 µs | 13:41:13 |

## Pool Wait

*Time clients spent queued for a server connection, a pool sizing signal rather than a query one. Averaged as the timings above are. What it is averaged over depends on pool_mode (one wait per session, per transaction or per statement), which pgBouncer logs nowhere.*

| Metric         | Weighted average | Max snapshot average |       At |
|----------------|-----------------:|---------------------:|---------:|
| Pool wait time |          331 µs |              331 µs | 13:41:13 |

